# CABLE UPPERCUT

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Cable Uppercut is an explosive resistance exercise designed to develop vertical force production, rotational coordination and upward power transfer through the kinetic chain.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-transfer resistance exercises for improving uppercut mechanics and close-range striking performance.

---

# Philosophy

A powerful uppercut is generated from the ground.

The legs initiate force, the hips rotate and extend, the trunk transfers energy, and the arm delivers the strike.

The Cable Uppercut overloads this kinetic chain while maintaining a movement pattern closely related to combat performance.

CAS uses the Cable Uppercut to improve explosive upward force production without excessive fatigue.

